      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`wallet_keypool_topup.py` is meant to test keypool restore for four output types, one node each. But the wallet and backup paths are only set for node1, so for nodes 2-4 the test copies node1's backup over node1's running wallet and restarts the node under test on its own, never-restored wallet. The checks still pass, so only the legacy case has actually been tested since 0dcac51049.\n\nThis backs up and restores each node's own wallet, and asserts that the restored wallet rescans on startup so the test can't silently skip the restore again. Adding just that assertion on master makes the test fail at node2.\n\nAlso fixes `wallet_createwallet.py` calling `w7.walletpassphrase` where it means w8 (since c5d3787367), so the `avoid_reuse wallet` was never checked.",
    "labels": [
