      "message": "test: restore each node's own wallet backup in wallet_keypool_topup\n\n0dcac51049 extended this test to check keypool restore for every output\ntype, one node each. However, the wallet and backup paths were only\ncomputed for node1, and only node1's wallet was backed up. For nodes\n2-4, the restore step copied node1's backup over node1's wallet while\nnode1 was running, then restarted the node under test on its own,\nnever-restored wallet. The p2sh-segwit, bech32 and bech32m checks\ntherefore passed trivially: that wallet had derived the keys and\nreceived the funds itself.\n\nBack up each node's wallet with backupwallet and restore that backup\ninto the node under test. Assert that the restored wallet rescans on\nstartup, so the test fails if a node is ever restarted without its\nbackup again. Also update the docstring, which still described the\noriginal two-node test.",
